{
 "about": "One response judged against one request and a reference. The CLI judges it with internal/interpret, the page with web/js/judge.js; both must produce the expected result. visibility full: every response header is readable (the CLI always; a same-origin fetch). visibility cors: only the headers a cross-origin page may read are present. Reference byte i is (167*i + 61*(i>>8) + 13) mod 256. body.ref [a,b] delivers reference bytes a..b (b<a: none); shift moves the source window; flip inverts the bytes at those body offsets; cut keeps only that many bytes; extra appends bytes that never match; error ends the body with that failure after the delivered bytes. A body shorter than the read limit ends with EOF unless error is set.",
 "vectors": [
  {
   "name": "206 head, correct bytes",
   "ref_size": 1000,
   "request": "bytes=0-99",
   "response": {
    "status": 206,
    "headers": {
     "Content-Range": "bytes 0-99/1000",
     "Content-Length": "100"
    }
   },
   "body": {
    "ref": [0, 99]
   },
   "expect": {
    "status": "pass",
    "findings": [],
    "bytes": "match",
    "encoding": "identity"
   }
  },
  {
